1
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:08,970
In the year 845, the Colossal Titan
and the Armored Titan suddenly appeared

2
00:00:09,180 --> 00:00:13,640
and destroyed one of humanity's
walls... and everyday life with it.

3
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:17,650
Humanity abandoned Wall Maria,

4
00:00:17,850 --> 00:00:21,270
lost 20% of its population
and one-third of its territory,

5
00:00:21,480 --> 00:00:25,820
and was forced to
retreat behind Wall Rose.

6
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:30,620
And then, in the year 850...

7
00:00:30,830 --> 00:00:33,080
Humanity's fight back...

8
00:00:33,290 --> 00:00:34,870
...is just beginning!

9
00:00:37,210 --> 00:00:40,380
The target is the
Colossal Titan dead ahead!

10
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:44,000
This is our chance!
Don't let it get away!

11
00:00:46,720 --> 00:00:48,130
Hey, there.

12
00:00:49,010 --> 00:00:51,140
It's been five years since we met.

13
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:12,240
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

14
00:01:12,450 --> 00:01:17,710
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

15
00:01:17,910 --> 00:01:22,790
Prayers won't solve anything

16
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:28,130
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

17
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:33,430
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

18
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:35,970
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

19
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,850
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

20
00:01:39,060 --> 00:01:44,230
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

21
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:49,530
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

22
00:01:49,740 --> 00:01:54,740
consumed with surging bloodlust,

23
00:01:54,950 --> 00:02:01,870
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

24
00:02:23,998 --> 00:02:29,003
First Battle: The Struggle for Trost, Part 1

25
00:02:50,050 --> 00:02:53,720
He went for the cannons!

26
00:02:54,720 --> 00:02:58,220
And he didn't take out
the gate by accident, either!

27
00:02:58,430 --> 00:03:03,190
He does have intelligence...!

28
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:10,650
Still, this is the perfect chance!

29
00:03:10,860 --> 00:03:13,490
He's the only one
who can destroy the wall!

30
00:03:15,410 --> 00:03:17,410
If I can just take him out...!

31
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:26,210
Too slow!

32
00:03:28,210 --> 00:03:30,130
Got you!

33
00:03:32,010 --> 00:03:33,420
Wha...?!

34
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:35,090
Hot!

35
00:03:42,770 --> 00:03:46,690
Go!

36
00:03:50,020 --> 00:03:51,530
I missed?!

37
00:03:57,110 --> 00:03:58,570
No...

38
00:03:58,780 --> 00:04:03,160
The Colossal Titan disappeared!

39
00:04:03,370 --> 00:04:06,000
Eren! Did you beat it?!

40
00:04:06,210 --> 00:04:08,130
No!

41
00:04:08,330 --> 00:04:10,130
It's just like five years ago!

42
00:04:10,340 --> 00:04:13,960
He suddenly appeared,
then suddenly disappeared!

43
00:04:16,760 --> 00:04:18,510
I'm sorry. I let him get away.

44
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:21,470
What are you apologizing for?
We were scared stiff...

45
00:04:21,680 --> 00:04:24,140
Hey! This is no time for that!

46
00:04:24,350 --> 00:04:26,020
The wall's been broken!

47
00:04:26,230 --> 00:04:29,480
We have to hurry and seal
it before the Titans get in again!

48
00:04:29,690 --> 00:04:31,150
What are you doing?!

49
00:04:31,360 --> 00:04:34,990
The Colossal Titan Response
Operation is already underway!

50
00:04:35,190 --> 00:04:36,650
Return to HQ at once!

51
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:39,450
Anyone who's come into contact
with it, remember to give a report!

52
00:04:39,660 --> 00:04:40,160
Yes, Sir!

53
00:04:40,370 --> 00:04:42,950
We pray for the
advance team's success!

54
00:04:59,090 --> 00:05:01,220
Take only the
absolute bare necessities!

55
00:05:01,430 --> 00:05:03,430
Please evacuate
in a calm manner!

56
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:08,940
If they break through here,

57
00:05:09,140 --> 00:05:13,070
we'll have another tragedy just
like five years ago on our hands!

58
00:05:13,270 --> 00:05:17,650
We must hold the Titans off here!

59
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:20,740
Prepare to intercept!

60
00:05:22,570 --> 00:05:23,990
Fire!

61
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:32,250
Charge!

62
00:05:35,340 --> 00:05:40,130
You cadets have successfully graduated!
You are now proper soldiers!

63
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:43,100
I have high hopes
for you in this operation!

64
00:05:43,930 --> 00:05:46,020
Don't worry, Hanna.

65
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,020
I promise I'll keep you safe.

66
00:05:48,230 --> 00:05:49,640
Franz...

67
00:05:53,150 --> 00:05:55,360
Are you okay, Armin?!

68
00:05:55,570 --> 00:05:57,570
I-I'm fine!

69
00:05:57,780 --> 00:06:00,200
I'll calm down soon enough!

70
00:06:00,400 --> 00:06:02,030
Still, this is bad!

71
00:06:02,240 --> 00:06:07,120
We don't have the technology to
quickly seal an 8-meter-high hole!

72
00:06:07,330 --> 00:06:12,960
And we never did manage to unearth
that big rock near the front gate!

73
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:18,130
Unless we seal the hole,
this city's as good as lost!

74
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:26,060
It's only a matter of time
until Wall Rose is breached!

75
00:06:26,260 --> 00:06:29,310
In fact, if they ever feel like it,

76
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,980
they can pretty much wipe
out humanity anytime they want!

77
00:06:32,190 --> 00:06:33,600
Armin!

78
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:36,980
Calm down! This isn't like last time!

79
00:06:37,190 --> 00:06:40,530
Humanity won't give in
to the Titans anymore!

80
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:46,990
I'm sorry...

81
00:06:47,200 --> 00:06:48,660
I'm all right...

82
00:07:04,220 --> 00:07:08,220
Come, now.
Are you playing seriously?

83
00:07:08,430 --> 00:07:12,850
There. I win again.

84
00:07:13,060 --> 00:07:20,440
We square off once a month, yet you
never seem to improve at all, Pyxis.

85
00:07:20,650 --> 00:07:25,740
Oh, no, I am just no
match for you, Lord Wald.

86
00:07:29,450 --> 00:07:34,460
You're the top officer in charge
of the entire southern territory.

87
00:07:37,460 --> 00:07:39,630
How do you hope
to triumph over the Titans

88
00:07:39,840 --> 00:07:41,760
with such paltry skill and intellect?

89
00:07:41,960 --> 00:07:43,510
Commander Pyxis!

90
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,050
I bring a message!

91
00:07:45,260 --> 00:07:47,050
How uncouth! Who are you...?!

92
00:07:47,260 --> 00:07:50,060
The Colossal Titan has appeared in Trost!

93
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:52,310
The gate has been destroyed!

94
00:08:04,700 --> 00:08:08,570
Mm. This is a fine drink, indeed.

95
00:08:08,780 --> 00:08:13,790
As a fellow warrior on the field
of battle, I will humbly accept it.

96
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:17,290
H-Hey! Wait, Pyxis!

97
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:21,460
Pyxis! Hey! Wait just a minute!

98
00:08:21,670 --> 00:08:24,670
I forbid you to leave!

99
00:08:24,880 --> 00:08:29,680
Assemble your troops
immediately and defend my domain!

100
00:08:29,890 --> 00:08:32,930
That is your duty!

101
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:36,640
Lord Wald.

102
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:41,610
As we speak, soldiers in Trost
are literally risking their lives in battle.

103
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:44,900
Commander.
I will ready the horses.

104
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:49,070
I presume many lives are
being lost as well.

105
00:08:49,280 --> 00:08:52,160
Right now, at this very moment.

106
00:08:52,370 --> 00:08:54,830
Hmph. Insignificant lives, I'm sure.

107
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:56,710
Forget about them.

108
00:08:56,910 --> 00:08:59,710
Your presence there
won't change anything anyway;

109
00:08:59,920 --> 00:09:03,960
you continually lose
to me in our tabletop skirmishes!

110
00:09:04,170 --> 00:09:06,670
Fear not, Your Lordship.

111
00:09:06,880 --> 00:09:09,220
Should he face the
Titans on a real battlefield,

112
00:09:09,430 --> 00:09:13,350
the commander will not
need to be as lenient with them.

113
00:09:15,140 --> 00:09:16,560
Enough.

114
00:09:17,680 --> 00:09:19,190
Lord Wald.

115
00:09:19,390 --> 00:09:24,780
Please have another pleasant and
peaceful day as always.

116
00:09:26,570 --> 00:09:28,200
H-Hey!

117
00:09:29,070 --> 00:09:30,280
Pyxis!

118
00:09:30,490 --> 00:09:33,160
Come back! Pyxis!

119
00:09:33,370 --> 00:09:35,660
Pyxis!

120
00:09:48,050 --> 00:09:50,840
As practiced,
you will now split into your squads

121
00:09:51,050 --> 00:09:55,010
and perform resupply, message
relay, and Titan-clearing duties

122
00:09:55,220 --> 00:09:58,020
under the command
of the Garrison Regiment!

123
00:09:58,230 --> 00:10:01,020
The Garrison Regiment's
intercept squad will take the vanguard!

124
00:10:01,020 --> 00:10:01,650
"Vanguard"

125
00:10:01,650 --> 00:10:04,020
"Vanguard"
"Middle Guard"
The Cadets, led by the support squad,
will take the middle guard!

126
00:10:04,020 --> 00:10:04,770
"Vanguard"
"Middle Guard"

127
00:10:04,770 --> 00:10:07,940
"Vanguard"
"Middle Guard"
"Rearguard"
And the Garrison Regiment's
elite squads will take the rearguard!

128
00:10:07,940 --> 00:10:08,190
"Vanguard"
"Middle Guard"
"Rearguard"

129
00:10:08,190 --> 00:10:09,820
Additionally, I've received word

130
00:10:10,030 --> 00:10:13,280
that the advance team
has been wiped out!

131
00:10:13,490 --> 00:10:17,370
The outer gate has been breached,
and the Titans have been allowed inside!

132
00:10:17,580 --> 00:10:21,920
In other words, the Armored Titan
could very well appear again

133
00:10:22,120 --> 00:10:25,130
and demolish the inner gate at any time!

134
00:10:26,420 --> 00:10:29,130
- You can't be serious...
- You gotta be kidding me...

135
00:10:29,340 --> 00:10:31,630
If they end up breaching Rose too...!

136
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:33,680
Quiet!

137
00:10:33,890 --> 00:10:36,640
The vanguard is currently
engaged with the enemy!

138
00:10:36,850 --> 00:10:38,970
This defense operation
has but one objective:

139
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:44,230
to defend Wall Rose until the
citizens have finished evacuating!

140
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:49,400
Also, as I'm sure you're well aware,
desertion is punishable by death!

141
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:51,820
Be prepared to lay down your lives!

142
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:53,160
Dismissed!

143
00:10:53,360 --> 00:10:54,780
Sir!

144
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:02,120
Why today?

145
00:11:02,330 --> 00:11:05,290
I would've been on my
way to the interior tomorrow...

146
00:11:07,170 --> 00:11:08,800
Are you okay?!

147
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:18,060
No, no, no, noooo...

148
00:11:24,390 --> 00:11:25,980
Move!

149
00:11:26,190 --> 00:11:27,980
Hey, Jean! What's wrong?!

150
00:11:28,190 --> 00:11:29,730
"What's wrong?!"

151
00:11:29,940 --> 00:11:33,110
That's easy for you to say,
you suicidal maniac!

152
00:11:33,320 --> 00:11:35,820
You want to join the Scouts!

153
00:11:36,030 --> 00:11:39,620
You're ready to
be Titan chow anytime!

154
00:11:39,830 --> 00:11:42,620
- But I was headed for the interior tomorrow!
- Calm down!

155
00:11:42,830 --> 00:11:44,620
You expect me to calm
down and accept death?!

156
00:11:44,830 --> 00:11:45,870
No!

157
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,500
Think back!

158
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:50,880
Think back to the three years
of sweat and blood we endured!

159
00:11:52,010 --> 00:11:55,510
So many times we came close
to dying during those three years!

160
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:57,680
Some people did die.

161
00:11:57,890 --> 00:12:01,010
Some ran off. Others were kicked out.

162
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,140
But we survived!

163
00:12:03,350 --> 00:12:04,560
Right?!

164
00:12:04,770 --> 00:12:08,020
I'm sure we can survive today, too!

165
00:12:09,150 --> 00:12:14,110
You can just survive today
and leave for the interior tomorrow!

166
00:12:18,570 --> 00:12:19,990
Damn!

167
00:12:21,790 --> 00:12:24,660
Let's go, Daz! Quit your damn cryin'!

168
00:12:24,870 --> 00:12:27,040
R-Right...

169
00:12:27,250 --> 00:12:28,670
Eren.

170
00:12:29,250 --> 00:12:32,050
If the battle gets chaotic,
come find me.

171
00:12:32,250 --> 00:12:35,550
Huh? We're in different squads!

172
00:12:35,760 --> 00:12:39,050
If the situation falls apart,
things won't go according to plan.

173
00:12:39,260 --> 00:12:40,600
I'll protect you!

174
00:12:40,800 --> 00:12:41,760
What the hell are you...

175
00:12:41,970 --> 00:12:44,180
Cadet Ackermann.

176
00:12:44,390 --> 00:12:46,140
You're in the rearguard. Special orders.

177
00:12:46,350 --> 00:12:47,140
Come with me.

178
00:12:47,350 --> 00:12:50,230
I-I'm not skilled enough!
I'll only be a burden!

179
00:12:51,400 --> 00:12:53,980
I am not asking for your opinion.

180
00:12:54,190 --> 00:12:55,900
The citizens' evacuation
is behind schedule.

181
00:12:56,110 --> 00:12:59,030
We need as many elite
soldiers near them as possible.

182
00:12:59,240 --> 00:13:00,950
- B-But...!
- Hey!

183
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:04,040
Cut the crap, Mikasa!

184
00:13:04,240 --> 00:13:06,580
Quit freaking out like everyone else!

185
00:13:06,790 --> 00:13:08,790
Humanity's on the
verge of extinction here!

186
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:12,340
This is no time to go and
impose your own selfish rules!

187
00:13:16,090 --> 00:13:20,680
I'm sorry. I wasn't thinking clearly.

188
00:13:21,890 --> 00:13:24,680
I do have one thing to ask.

189
00:13:27,730 --> 00:13:30,190
Please don't die.

190
00:13:37,190 --> 00:13:40,450
I ain't gonna die.

191
00:13:40,660 --> 00:13:42,950
I can't die yet!

192
00:13:45,620 --> 00:13:50,250
Because I still don't know
what this world is really like!

193
00:13:53,420 --> 00:13:58,630
Surviving historical documents
say nothing about the origin of the Titans.

194
00:13:58,840 --> 00:14:01,510
Most everything remains unknown.

195
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:04,720
The things we do know about now,
including Titan ecology,

196
00:14:04,930 --> 00:14:08,730
are based entirely on the latest
reports from the Scout Regiment.

197
00:14:08,930 --> 00:14:12,900
We've been unable to determine if
the Titans possess human-like intelligence.

198
00:14:13,100 --> 00:14:18,440
As such, there've been no cases
to date of mutual communication.

199
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:23,530
Titan physiology is fundamentally
different from that of other living beings.

200
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:27,990
They lack reproductive organs,
and it is unclear how they reproduce,

201
00:14:28,200 --> 00:14:31,500
but they primarily possess male-like physiques.

202
00:14:31,710 --> 00:14:34,380
They have extremely
high body temperatures,

203
00:14:34,580 --> 00:14:39,670
and, perplexingly enough, they show
no interest in anything but humans.

204
00:14:40,970 --> 00:14:44,720
Consuming people is the
Titans' sole principle of behavior,

205
00:14:44,930 --> 00:14:51,270
but given that they've existed for over
a century in a human-less environment,

206
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:56,230
we can surmise that the very act
of feeding is unnecessary for them.

207
00:14:56,440 --> 00:15:00,440
In other words, it's believed that
they are not motivated by predation,

208
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:02,320
but by bloodlust.

209
00:15:03,610 --> 00:15:08,290
And, most of all, the Titans'
tremendous vitality is the primary reason

210
00:15:08,490 --> 00:15:12,120
that humankind has been
so greatly overwhelmed.

211
00:15:12,330 --> 00:15:15,500
Humanity has long
possessed cannon technology,

212
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:18,550
but that alone wasn't
enough to combat them.

213
00:15:18,750 --> 00:15:21,920
Even when their heads are
blown off, the Titans don't die.

214
00:15:22,130 --> 00:15:23,930
Additionally, although
there is some variability,

215
00:15:24,130 --> 00:15:27,550
their heads will fully regenerate
in only a minute or two.

216
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,100
You can't be serious...

217
00:15:29,310 --> 00:15:31,140
Their size is bad enough as it is...

218
00:15:31,350 --> 00:15:34,440
Sir! Does that mean
the Titans are immortal?!

219
00:15:35,770 --> 00:15:37,560
They are not immortal.

220
00:15:37,770 --> 00:15:40,900
There is one way to defeat a Titan.

221
00:15:41,110 --> 00:15:43,030
You target here.

222
00:15:43,240 --> 00:15:49,200
When severely damaged here,
a Titan will die without regenerating.

223
00:15:49,410 --> 00:15:53,960
That's where these two
flesh-paring blades come in.

224
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:57,000
A successful strike to a
Titan's weak spot with these

225
00:15:57,210 --> 00:16:02,550
will cause its immediate death,
with no time to regenerate whatsoever.

226
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:11,180
Hey, Armin.

227
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:13,980
This is the perfect chance, don't you think?

228
00:16:14,980 --> 00:16:19,730
If we take care of business in this first
battle before we've even joined the Scouts,

229
00:16:19,940 --> 00:16:24,320
we rookies will shoot up
the ranks for sure!

230
00:16:30,950 --> 00:16:33,450
Yeah. No question about it.

231
00:16:33,660 --> 00:16:36,710
Just so you know,
you aren't the only ones in our class

232
00:16:36,920 --> 00:16:38,710
who wanna join the Scouts.

233
00:16:38,920 --> 00:16:42,800
You beat us to the punch earlier,
but you won't outdo us this time!

234
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,760
Sounds like a challenge, Thomas!

235
00:16:44,960 --> 00:16:48,010
Whoever takes out the most Titans wins!

236
00:16:48,220 --> 00:16:51,140
- Don't go messin' with the scores!
- Squad 34, move out!

237
00:16:51,350 --> 00:16:53,310
Bolster the vanguard!

238
00:16:54,350 --> 00:16:56,560
All right! Let's go!

239
00:17:20,040 --> 00:17:21,920
That many Titans?!

240
00:17:22,130 --> 00:17:24,420
The Vanguard's been totally routed!

241
00:17:24,630 --> 00:17:28,590
What are they doing?!
Those hot shots usually act all tough!

242
00:17:28,800 --> 00:17:33,180
I figured things would
be bad, but not like this!

243
00:17:34,260 --> 00:17:36,060
An Abnormal!

244
00:17:36,270 --> 00:17:37,680
Stop!

245
00:17:54,370 --> 00:17:55,790
Huh...?

246
00:18:20,520 --> 00:18:22,770
What the hell are you doing?!

247
00:18:22,980 --> 00:18:25,690
- Eren!
- Don't go off on your own!

248
00:18:29,030 --> 00:18:31,700
Get back here, damn it!

249
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:33,910
You're gonna pay for killing Thomas!

250
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:38,160
I won't let you get away! I won't!

251
00:18:48,460 --> 00:18:49,670
Eren!

252
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:51,420
Eren!

253
00:19:07,480 --> 00:19:11,110
Stop! Please don't!

254
00:19:17,080 --> 00:19:20,370
Why...?

255
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:24,830
Why am I watching
as my friends get eaten?

256
00:19:31,550 --> 00:19:36,260
Why... can't I move...?

257
00:19:47,230 --> 00:19:49,230
A-Armin...

258
00:19:50,980 --> 00:19:53,900
Eren! Eren!

259
00:19:54,110 --> 00:19:55,530
Eren!

260
00:19:57,240 --> 00:19:58,320
What is it, Armin?

261
00:19:58,530 --> 00:20:01,790
My grandpa secretly had this!

262
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:05,210
It's a book about the outside world!

263
00:20:05,420 --> 00:20:07,750
A book about the outside world?!

264
00:20:07,960 --> 00:20:11,800
Isn't it illegal to have those?
You're gonna get arrested!

265
00:20:12,010 --> 00:20:14,800
This is no time to be saying that!

266
00:20:15,010 --> 00:20:15,970
According to this book,

267
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:20,140
most of the world is covered
in water called a "sea"!

268
00:20:20,350 --> 00:20:22,970
And this "sea" is entirely saltwater!

269
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:24,270
Salt?!

270
00:20:24,480 --> 00:20:27,850
Y-You're lying!
Salt is a treasure trove!

271
00:20:28,060 --> 00:20:30,400
I'm sure merchants
would've snatched it all up!

272
00:20:30,610 --> 00:20:33,280
You can't, though! The sea is that big!

273
00:20:33,480 --> 00:20:35,490
Yeah, right...

274
00:20:35,700 --> 00:20:38,240
There's a lot more than loads of salt, too!

275
00:20:38,450 --> 00:20:42,740
Fiery water! Lands of ice!
Sandy snowfields!

276
00:20:42,950 --> 00:20:45,040
The outside world
must be many times larger

277
00:20:45,250 --> 00:20:47,830
than the inside of these walls!

278
00:20:48,040 --> 00:20:50,380
The outside world...

279
00:20:50,590 --> 00:20:53,760
And, this is still a secret,

280
00:20:53,960 --> 00:20:58,760
but my mom and dad are planning
to venture into the outside world!

281
00:20:58,970 --> 00:21:01,140
The outside world, huh...

282
00:21:01,350 --> 00:21:03,100
Hey, Eren.

283
00:21:03,310 --> 00:21:08,390
I hope we can explore
the outside world too someday!

284
00:21:26,960 --> 00:21:28,370
Eren!

285
00:21:29,420 --> 00:21:33,420
I refuse to die here...

286
00:21:35,710 --> 00:21:39,220
Listen, Armin...

287
00:21:39,430 --> 00:21:43,720
You told me about it...

288
00:21:43,930 --> 00:21:47,520
So I have... to see it...

289
00:21:47,730 --> 00:21:50,730
The outside world...!

290
00:21:52,060 --> 00:21:53,230
Eren!

291
00:21:53,440 --> 00:21:54,860
Hurry!

292
00:22:36,440 --> 00:22:41,360
Your dreams are where your heart is

293
00:22:41,570 --> 00:22:47,620
They're more fragile than life itself

294
00:22:47,830 --> 00:22:52,290
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

295
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:58,960
Now, rest in peace

296
00:22:59,170 --> 00:23:10,310
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

297
00:23:10,520 --> 00:23:20,570
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

298
00:23:20,780 --> 00:23:26,530
In this beautiful, cruel world

299
00:23:26,740 --> 00:23:31,700
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

300
00:23:31,910 --> 00:23:37,420
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

301
00:23:37,630 --> 00:23:43,090
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

302
00:23:43,300 --> 00:23:46,720
to anything anymore?

303
00:23:53,640 --> 00:23:55,770
Suddenly, it begins to rain.

304
00:23:55,980 --> 00:23:57,810
The quiet sound of the rainfall...

305
00:23:58,020 --> 00:24:02,650
The damp air...
The faintly sweet smell of rain...

306
00:24:02,860 --> 00:24:04,923
They remind Mikasa of
a ghastly incident in her past.

307
00:24:04,923 --> 00:24:06,740
The World the Girl Saw: The Struggle for Trost, Part 2
They remind Mikasa of
a ghastly incident in her past.

308
00:24:06,740 --> 00:24:06,925
The World the Girl Saw: The Struggle for Trost, Part 2
